statement.paragraph:
A particle moving in a planar force field has a position vector $\textbf{x}$ that satisfies $\mathbf{x}\prime = A\textbf{x}$. The $2 \times 2$ matrix $A$ has eigenvalues $4$ and $2$, with corresponding eigenvectors $\textbf{v}_{1} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 3} \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$ and $\textbf{v}_{2} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Find the position of the particle at time $t$, assuming that $\textbf{x}(0) = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 6} \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$.

Let $A$ be a $2 \times 2$ matrix with eigenvalues $- 3$ and $- 1$ and corresponding eigenvectors $\textbf{v}_{1} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      {- 1} \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$ and $\textbf{v}_{2} = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      1 \\
      1
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$. Let $\textbf{x}(t)$ be the position of a particle at time $t$. Solve the initial value problem $\mathbf{x}\prime = A\textbf{x}$, $\textbf{x}(0) = \left\lbrack \begin{array}{r}
      2 \\
      3
      \end{array} \right\rbrack$.

